// =============================================================================
// OpenCode gateway-isolated third-party provider — template only (v2 schema)
// =============================================================================
// Use this when you want a third-party provider's real key to stay on the
// VM instead of in the sandbox. OpenCode v2 config shape: the top-level key
// is `providers` (plural), the adapter is chosen with `package`, the
// endpoint lives in `settings`, and credentials are declared via `env` —
// a v1-format block (singular `provider` + `options.*`) is silently
// ignored by v2.
//
// 1. Add the real key on the Mac:
//      ~/.ai-secrets/ai-gateway.env
//      REAL_FOO_API_KEY=...
//
// 2. Uncomment the /foo block in gateway/Caddyfile and set:
//      handle_path /foo/* {
//          reverse_proxy https://api.foo.com {
//              header_up Host api.foo.com
//              header_up Authorization "Bearer {env.REAL_FOO_API_KEY}"
//          }
//      }
//    Apply: just seed-secrets && just gateway-reload
//    (copies the Caddyfile to the VM, validates it, restarts the gateway)
//
// 3. Copy the provider block below into your OpenCode config
//    (~/.config/opencode/opencode.json or a project opencode.json).
//    The base URL is:
//      provider origin           https://api.foo.com/v1
//      gateway origin            http://host.docker.internal:4000/foo/v1
//    Keep the native path after the route; the gateway forwards it
//    unchanged.
//
// 4. Put the dummy key in the FOO_API_KEY env var (that project's .ai.env,
//    or compose) — v2 reads credentials from env, not from the config file.
//
// 5. The gateway is protocol-blind. For an Anthropic-style provider, use
//    the matching @opencode/ai provider package and add x-api-key to the
//    Caddy template if the provider expects that header instead of Bearer.
// =============================================================================
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "providers": {
    "foo": {
      "name": "Foo (via gateway)",
      "env": ["FOO_API_KEY"],
      "package": "@opencode/ai/providers/openai-compatible",
      "settings": {
        "baseURL": "http://host.docker.internal:4000/foo/v1"
      },
      "models": {
        "foo-model": {
          "name": "Foo Model"
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
